.TH BNLEARN 1 2000-1月 "wildtype_baseline" "wildtype_baseline"
.SH NAME
wildtype_baseline \- set wildtype baseline
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIwildtype_baseline(\fBmodel\fR as any, 
\fBbaseline\fR as list, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
set wildtype baseline
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBmodel\fB \fR\- 
 [BNLearnWorkflow](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.BNLearn.Core.BNLearnWorkflow), [BlockBayesianNetwork](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.BNLearn.ModularNetwork.BlockBayesianNetwork), or the elastic net
 perturbation engine that is created via \fBlinear::elastic_model\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBbaseline\fB \fR\- a value list tuple of the baseline expression value, example as list(gene1=xxx,gene2=xxx,...). 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- -. 
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
For the elastic net engine the given values are interpreted in the model space
 (i.e. the same numeric space as the expression matrix that was used to fit the network),
 and the genes that are not modelled are simply ignored.
.PP
